  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The granular neighborhood analysis focuses on a single district within Madrid, which may limit how directly the specific spatial trajectories apply to cities with different economic geographies.",
      "what": "Using circular statistics, the study analyzed spatial directionality and temporal patterns in new restaurant openings across Madrid, Spain, between 2018 and 2024, focusing closely on the Ríos Rosas neighborhood. The analysis revealed a dominant expansion vector toward the city's economically dynamic northern sector alongside recurring seasonal opening cycles.",
      "why": "It introduces a circular statistical approach to quantify spatial directionality and temporal rhythms in restaurant clustering, providing a method to track urban foodification as it moves through specific corridors over time."
